{id:'d2',ch:'docs',type:'w',
 q:'You have a vendor PDF for a new relay board. Describe the complete workflow to make it appear as a block in the Silmulator library — from the PDF to the running app.',
 c:[{l:'put PDF in hardware_docs/<vendor>/<model>/',t:['hardware_docs','pdf','vendor','folder']},
    {l:'write scpi_commands.md (optional but recommended)',t:['scpi_commands','markdown','md','command table']},
    {l:'create JSON spec in silmulator/custom_blocks/',t:['custom_blocks','json','spec']},
    {l:'restart app — discover_specs() picks it up',t:['restart','discover_specs','startup','launch']}],
 m:`1. Place the vendor PDF in hardware_docs/<vendor>/<model>/programmer_reference.pdf (e.g. hardware_docs/mylab/relay-4ch/).
2. (Recommended) Write a scpi_commands.md in that folder summarising only the commands you'll actually test — this is the human reference the JSON spec is derived from.
3. Create a JSON spec file in silmulator/custom_blocks/mylab_relay4ch.json with the block's name, color, ports, and commands map.
4. Restart Silmulator. At import time, register_custom_blocks() calls discover_specs() which globs *.json in both PACKAGED_DIR and USER_DIR, parses each spec, and calls make_custom_block_class(spec) to synthesise a live Python class — then adds it to BLOCK_REGISTRY. The block appears in the Library panel.`
},

{id:'d3',ch:'docs',type:'w',
 q:'What are the two directories that discover_specs() scans? What is the difference between them in terms of who should use each?',
 snip:`<span class="cm"># custom_block.py</span>
PACKAGED_DIR = Path(__file__)...parent.parent.parent / <span class="str">"custom_blocks"</span>
USER_DIR = Path.home() / <span class="str">".silmulator"</span> / <span class="str">"custom_blocks"</span>`,
 c:[{l:'PACKAGED_DIR = silmulator/custom_blocks/ (shipped in repo)',t:['packaged','silmulator/custom_block','repo','shipped','project']},
    {l:'USER_DIR = ~/.silmulator/custom_blocks/ (personal/local)',t:['user_dir','~/.silmulator','home','personal','local']},
    {l:'PACKAGED for team/shared; USER_DIR for personal blocks',t:['team','shared','personal','individual','per-user']}],
 m:`PACKAGED_DIR = silmulator/custom_blocks/ — inside the repo. These specs are committed to version control and ship with the installer, Docker image, and .app bundle. Use this for blocks the whole team needs.
USER_DIR = ~/.silmulator/custom_blocks/ — in the user's home directory. These are personal or experimental blocks that aren't committed. Only that machine sees them; other team members won't have them unless they copy the file manually. Useful for work-in-progress specs before they're polished enough to commit.`
