{id:'c1',ch:'custom',type:'w',
 q:'A custom block JSON has this command entry: "ECHO": "echo:{0}". What does _make_handler do with this template, and what does the block return when a user sends "ECHO 42"?',
 snip:`<span class="cm"># custom_block.py:114</span>
<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">_make_handler</span>(template):
    <span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">handler</span>(cmd):
        <span class="kw">if not</span> template: <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="str">""</span>
        <span class="kw">if</span> <span class="str">"{"</span> <span class="kw">not in</span> template: <span class="kw">return</span> template
        <span class="kw">try</span>: <span class="kw">return</span> template.<span class="fn">format</span>(*cmd.params)
        <span class="kw">except</span>: <span class="kw">return</span> template
    <span class="kw">return</span> handler`,
 c:[{l:'template.format(*cmd.params) substitutes SCPI params',t:['format','cmd.params','params','substitute','{0}']},
    {l:'"ECHO 42" → cmd.params = ["42"] → echo:42',t:['echo:42','42','echo:']},
    {l:'empty template → write-only (returns "")',t:['empty','write-only','""','no response']},
    {l:'no { in template → return verbatim',t:['no {','verbatim','literal','no brace']}],
 m:`_make_handler(template) is a closure factory. For "echo:{0}":
- "{" is in the template, so the format path runs.
- For "ECHO 42", the SCPI parser produces cmd.params = ["42"].
- template.format(*["42"]) → "echo:{0}".format("42") → "echo:42"
So the block responds with "echo:42".
The three branches: (1) empty string → write-only, returns ""; (2) no "{" → always return the template verbatim (e.g. "STATUS?": "OK" always returns "OK"); (3) "{0}", "{1}", etc. → substitute positional SCPI params.`
},

