{id:'c4',ch:'custom',type:'mc',
 q:'discover_specs() uses seen_names to deduplicate. What problem does this solve?',
 opts:[
  {t:'Prevents the same block name appearing twice if a spec in USER_DIR has the same name as one in PACKAGED_DIR.',c:true, w:'Correct. PACKAGED_DIR is scanned first. If USER_DIR has a spec with the same name, it\'s skipped. This lets the packaged version take precedence, preventing accidental override of shipped blocks.'},
  {t:'Prevents two specs that define the same SCPI command from conflicting at runtime.',c:false,w:'SCPI command conflicts are within a single device\'s _handlers dict. seen_names deduplicates at the spec/block level, not the command level.'},
  {t:'Prevents the same JSON file from being parsed twice if it appears in both dirs.',c:false,w:'A file appearing in both dirs would be the same content but with different paths, and the same name — so seen_names does catch this, but the reason is to handle the user-override scenario, not duplicate file paths.'},
  {t:'Ensures block names are valid Python identifiers before make_custom_block_class() uses them.',c:false,w:'make_custom_block_class() doesn\'t require Python-identifier names. seen_names is purely for deduplication, not validation.'},
 ]
},

{id:'c5',ch:'custom',type:'w',
 q:'What does make_custom_block_class(spec) return, and how does the resulting object end up callable as a zero-arg constructor in the BLOCK_REGISTRY?',
 c:[{l:'returns a new Python class (type)',t:['class','type','returns a class','new class']},
    {l:'__init__ calls super().__init__(_CustomDevice(spec), spec.name)',t:['_customdevice','super().__init__','device','spec.name']},
    {l:'class stored in BLOCK_REGISTRY[spec.name]',t:['block_registry','registry','spec.name']]},
    {l:'add_block() does cls() — zero-arg instantiation',t:['cls()','add_block','zero-arg','no arg']}],
 m:`make_custom_block_class(spec) returns a new Python class (created dynamically via a class statement inside the function). The class inherits from BaseBlock and its __init__ calls super().__init__(_CustomDevice(spec), spec.name) — wiring up a device whose SCPI handlers come from the spec's commands map.
register_custom_blocks() stores this class in BLOCK_REGISTRY[spec.name]. When add_block("Relay Board") is called, it does cls = BLOCK_REGISTRY["Relay Board"] then block = cls() — a zero-arg constructor call. The class's __init__ takes no arguments (spec is captured via closure), so this works transparently alongside the built-in block classes.`
},

